%[text] # Plotting Polar Energyscape Info
%[text] The `plotPolarEnergyscape` function creates advanced 2D polar coordinate visualizations of acoustic imaging data from CLAIT beamforming algorithms. It transforms rectangular acoustic images into intuitive polar plots with sophisticated visual enhancement options including intensity modulation, dynamic range control, and customizable color mapping.
%[text] This function is designed to work seamlessly with acoustic images generated by `clait.calculateAcousticImage()`, providing publication-ready visualizations of beamforming results.
%%
%[text] ## Namespace and Calling
%[text] The function is part of the CLAIT toolbox namespace and should be called using the full namespace qualifier:
clait.plotPolarEnergyscape(imageData, structSensor, structImage, options) 
%[text] ### Function Signatures
%[text] The function supports two calling modes: 
%[text] #### Plotting Mode
[hPlot, hCbar] = clait.plotPolarEnergyscape(imageData, structSensor, structImage, options) 
%[text] #### Options Query Mode
opts = clait.plotPolarEnergyscape('options') 
%%
%[text] ## Input Parameters
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Parameter** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `imageData` | 2D double array | Yes | Acoustic image from CLAIT beamforming \[numRangeBins × numAzimuthDirections\] |
%[text] | `structSensor` | struct | Yes | Sensor array configuration and signal characteristics |
%[text] | `structImage` | struct | Yes | Image formation parameters including azimuth angles |
%[text] | `options` | struct | No | Visualization customization parameters (see detailed breakdown) |
%[text:table]
%[text] 
%[text] ### **Detailed Breakdown of Input Structures**
%[text] #### 1. imageData
%[text] The 2D acoustic image matrix generated by `clait.calculateAcousticImage()`.
%[text] - **Dimensions**: `[numRangeBins × numAzimuthDirections]`
%[text] - **Type**: Double array
%[text] - **Content**: Beamformed intensity values representing acoustic reflections at different ranges and azimuth angles \
%[text] #### 2. structSensor
%[text] Structure containing sensor array setup and signal characteristics, you can use the same one as used for `clait.calculateAcousticImage()`:
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Field** | **Type** | **Description** | **Units** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `sampleRate` | scalar | ADC sampling frequency | Hz |
%[text] | `numSamplesSensor` | scalar | Total number of samples in acquisition | samples |
%[text] | `speedOfSound` | scalar | Speed of sound in medium (default: 343) | m/s |
%[text:table]
%[text] #### 
%[text] #### 3. structImage
%[text] Structure containing image formation parameters, you can use the same one as used for `clait.calculateAcousticImage()`:
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Field** | **Type** | **Description** | **Units** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `directionsAzimuth` | vector | Azimuth angles for image columns \[numDirections × 1\] | degrees |
%[text] | `decimationFactor` | scalar | Decimation factor applied to acoustic image (default: 10, as `calculateAcousticImage`) | dimensionless |
%[text:table]
%[text] #### 
%[text] #### 4. options (Optional)
%[text] Structure containing visualization parameters. Use `clait.plotPolarEnergyscape('options')` to retrieve all available options with defaults.
%[text] **Plot Style Options:**
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Field** | **Type** | **Default** | **Description** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `useSimplePlot` | logical | `false` | `true` = basic pcolor plot, `false` = intensity-modulated visualization |
%[text] | `useDbScale` | logical | `true` | `true` = dB scale, `false` = linear scale |
%[text] | `dbCut` | scalar | `-60` | Lower dB limit relative to peak (dB) |
%[text] | `dbMax` | scalar | `0` | Upper dB limit relative to peak (dB) |
%[text] | `linearMin` | scalar | `0` | Minimum value for linear scale normalization |
%[text] | `linearMax` | scalar | `1` | Maximum value for linear scale normalization |
%[text] | `normalizeToMax` | logical | `true` | Normalize data to its maximum value |
%[text] | `colormap` | N×3 array | `jet(1024)` | Colormap matrix |
%[text] | `backgroundColor` | color spec | `'w'` | Background color |
%[text] | `gridColor` | RGB or string | `[0.7 0.7 0.7]` | Grid line color |
%[text:table]
%[text] 
%[text] **Intensity Modulation Options** (only used when `useSimplePlot = false`):
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Field** | **Type** | **Default** | **Description** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `rangeCompensation` | scalar | `2` | Range compensation exponent (R^n) for spherical spreading |
%[text] | `angleCompStrength` | scalar | `3` | Angle compensation strength factor for beam pattern |
%[text] | `tanhScale` | scalar | `0.1` | Tanh scaling factor for intensity (soft clipping) |
%[text] | `tanhOffset` | scalar | `0.5` | Tanh offset for intensity |
%[text] | `intensityPower` | scalar | `0.15` | Power transform exponent for contrast control |
%[text:table]
%[text] 
%[text] **Grid Display Options:**
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Field** | **Type** | **Default** | **Description** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `showGrid` | logical | `true` | Display polar grid overlay |
%[text] | `gridRangeSpacing` | scalar | `0.5` | Spacing between range circles (m) |
%[text] | `gridAzimuthSpacing` | scalar | `15` | Spacing between azimuth lines (degrees) |
%[text:table]
%[text] 
%[text] **Display and Labeling Options:**
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Field** | **Type** | **Default** | **Description** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `showColorbar` | logical | `true` | Display colorbar |
%[text] | `xlabel` | string | `'Cross Range (m)'` | X-axis label |
%[text] | `ylabel` | string | `''` | Y-axis label |
%[text] | `title` | string | `''` | Plot title |
%[text:table]
%[text] 
%[text] **Performance Options:**
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Field** | **Type** | **Default** | **Description** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `rangeSubsample` | scalar | `1` | Range subsampling factor (1 = no subsample) |
%[text:table]
%%
%[text] ## Output
%[text:table]
%[text] | **Output** | **Type** | **Description** |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `hPlot` | graphics handle | Handle to the pcolor plot object |
%[text] | `hCbar` | graphics handle | Handle to the colorbar object, or `[]` if colorbar is not shown |
%[text:table]
%%
%[text] ## Examples
%[text] A full example is available, to quickly open it after installing the toolbox, run the following command:
clait.openClaitPlottingPolarEnergyscapeExample

